Z||000002||GSXPete||08-22-2001||11:08 PM||||hmmm...i say replace the cable. my gas pedal started to stick one day in my gsx, but i just ignored it. later at night on my way home, i floored it (for one last blast before i pull in) and the wire frayed so much, the throttle stuck at WOT and i was left in neutral at 9k rpm!! luckely i didn't blow anything. it was easy to get home because i was a block away, and it was downhill   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> hehe<p>[This message has been edited by GSXPete (edited 08-22-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||MooCow||08-23-2001||12:08 AM||||It feels lke the pedal is sticking itslef but Im not sure.  Won't be able to find out till morning.  Where do I get a new cable from??  Also if I hit the gas hard while driving to accelerate the pedal will get stuck untill I hit it again with my foot.  I know for a fact that nothing is grabbing it.<P>Thanks Ken||||reg||1
Z||000004||Indiana_resto_guy||08-23-2001||07:47 AM||||I would clean the pivot point at the throttle body first!||||reg||1
Z||000005||Alex4mula||08-23-2001||08:50 AM||||I have similar problems on both of my Formulas but still very minor to be anoying. One sticks a little open and the other is a little stiff. Heard that changing it is big PITA. I guess Fiero Store should have the cable. Would like to know any other source (cheaper).<P>------------------<BR>    Alex4mula<BR>:) Red & White (:<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.zing.com/picture/p69fbfe3e99ec5a0b81c10afcc578ff95/fe6d5c42.jpg.orig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000006||84Bill||08-23-2001||12:14 PM||||Try spraying some lube down the cable end. I had a very stiff cable, I had to actually move my seat faward and use my leg to push it down instead of my foot. I sprayed some WD40 down the tube ad tied the end up to the trunk so the fluid would run down. It worked very well and the pedal is not nearly as hard to push down.||||reg||1
Z||000007||stsmithgt||08-23-2001||12:56 PM||||If it's the cable sticking, replace it.  It's not worth the aggrevation and safety hazard of a sticking throttle cable.  They're not too expensive and not hard to put in.  You can clean out the rappers that have fallen past your ashtray while the console is off too.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  Believe me, I like my new cable a lot better.<P>If it's the throttle body where it's sticking, that's another story for someone else to tell.<P>------------------<BR>My work of art.(in progress.)    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/carpicsig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000008||85fierogt||08-23-2001||07:35 PM|||| the fiero store sells replacemnt cables for like 20 bucks no big deal ||||reg||1
